 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "bava_kamma.100b.4",
   "daf": "100b",
   "sentenceId": 3,
   "he": "גְּמָ׳ מַאי ״כָּאוּר״? אָמַר רַב נַחְמָן אָמַר רַבָּה בַּר בַּר חָנָה: כַּלְבּוֹס. מַאי כַּלְבּוֹס? אָמַר רַבָּה בַּר שְׁמוּאֵל:",
   "en": "«GEMARA:» The Gemara clarifies: «What» does the mishna mean by «unattractively? Rav Naḥman said» that «Rabba bar bar Ḥana said: Kelabus.» The Gemara asks: «What» does «kelabus» mean? «Rabba bar Shmuel said:»"
  },
  {
   "id": "bava_kamma.101a.1",
   "daf": "101a",
   "sentenceId": 0,
   "he": "כַּפְרָא דּוּדֵי.",
   "en": "«The sediments» of dye in «the cauldrons,» that is, the dyer took the dye remaining in the cauldron from previous use, and used that dye for this garment, leading to an inferior result."
  }
 ],
